{"continue":true}
== PreToolUse: a write to the loop's own state
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"PreToolUse","permissionDecision":"deny","permissionDecisionReason":".sdlc/state/active is protected while a story is being worked on: it is either human-owned configuration or the loop's own record of what happened. Instead: configuration is yours to change by hand outside a running iteration, and loop state changes through the sdlc command [write-protected-path]"}}
== PreToolUse: a write outside the repository
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"PreToolUse","permissionDecision":"deny","permissionDecisionReason":"this path is outside the repository, and the loop only governs what it can review. Instead: work inside the repository; if you need a file elsewhere, ask the user to create it [write-outside-repository]"}}
== PreToolUse: an edit from another session of the same project
{"continue":true}
== PreToolUse: a command that pushes
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"PreToolUse","permissionDecision":"deny","permissionDecisionReason":"`git push` writes refs, into this repository or from it, and a held story moves none; while a story is held, nothing its session runs moves trunk or a story branch, the story's own or another's, other than the story's own gated commit. Instead: leave branches to the loop: `sdlc stop` in a finished story's worktree lands it on trunk, and a person moves, deletes, pushes or fetches a branch in their own terminal; to read one, use `git log`, `git show` or `git diff` [branch-through-the-tool]"}}
== PreToolUse: a command that turns enforcement off
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"PreToolUse","permissionDecision":"deny","permissionDecisionReason":"SDLC_ENFORCE decides whether the loop is enforced at all, and it is set by the person who started the session, not from inside it. Instead: if a rule is wrong, say which one and why, and stop [enforcement-stays-on]"}}
== PreToolUse: a command that writes the loop's own state
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"PreToolUse","permissionDecision":"deny","permissionDecisionReason":".sdlc/state is the loop's own record, and a shell command is the one way around every rule that protects it. Instead: the sdlc command owns this: `sdlc artifact write` for a gate's documents, `sdlc review add` for a review, `sdlc gate` for an outcome; the freeze is lifted by the person running the session [loop-state-through-the-tool]"}}
